=== eligibility: every gate, one input per eligible final-Deferred candidate ===
OK   BASIC ELIGIBLE: pressured + finally Deferred + real contention + one final owner + all above-pressure dimensions tie -> exactly one PromotionInput for B with owner A
OK   PRESSURE NONE: the same authority with pressure NONE produces no input (NONE can never enter a promotion evaluation)
OK   MISSING PRESSURE: no pressure on record fails closed -- pressure is never inferred
OK   CONTENDED THEN PROPOSED: a pressured candidate that contended but is finally Proposed produces no input
OK   NO CONTENTION: a pressured final Deferred candidate with no trace event produces no input (a Deferred reason is not contention)
OK   NO FINAL OWNER: the historical owner is no longer Proposed -> no input
OK   OWNER ABSENT FROM THE FINAL RESULT ENTIRELY is valid history, not an owner: no input
OK   IMPORTANCE BLOCK: a HIGH owner against a pressured MEDIUM loser -> no input; a LOW-vs-HIGH loser likewise
OK   DEADLINE-TODAY BLOCK: an owner whose deadline is today blocks, even against a higher-importance loser
OK   DEADLINE BLOCK: with deadline-today and importance tied, an owner with a stronger (present / earlier) deadline blocks
OK   LOSER-STRONGER ANOMALY: a loser that outranks its final owner above pressure is an anomaly, never authority -> no input
OK   UNKNOWN PRECEDENCE: missing facts for the loser, or for a final owner, -> no input
OK   ORIGINALORDER-ONLY: the facts carry no originalOrder, so candidates that differ only by it (the only dimension pressure is meant to precede) still produce an input
OK   DUPLICATE IDS fail closed: a loser appearing twice in the final result, or a historical owner appearing twice, -> no input
OK   ROUND IS NEVER READ: the same authority with any round numbers (including malformed / negative ones) yields the identical input
OK   ATTEMPTED INTERVALS AND EVENT COUNTS ARE NEVER READ: three events over different intervals and rounds for the same owner give the same single-owner input as one event
=== owners: 1..N, deduplicated, final only, all-owner rule, never collapsed ===
OK   MULTI-OWNER ALL-TIE: two final owners that both tie above pressure -> ONE input carrying BOTH owners (never collapsed to a single winner), in order of first appearance in the trace
OK   owner order follows first appearance in the trace, not the final-result or alphabetical order
OK   MULTI-OWNER MIXED: one owner ties, the other is stronger -> no input (the all-owner rule is mandatory)
OK   MULTI-OWNER ANOMALY: one owner ties, the other is WEAKER above pressure (loser stronger) -> no input; an anomaly is never hidden by a tying owner
OK   MULTI-OWNER UNKNOWN: a final owner without precedence facts voids the input even though the other owner ties
OK   REPEATED OWNER / MULTI-ROUND OWNER: one owner across several events and rounds is ONE owner entry
OK   HISTORICAL OWNER REMOVED: A1 (stronger, but no longer Proposed) neither blocks nor appears; the remaining tied FINAL owner A2 is the only owner entry
OK   ALL OWNERS REMOVED: every historical owner displaced -> no input
OK   only the loser's OWN contention relationships define owners: an unrelated Proposed candidate (even one tying above pressure) is never an owner
